WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:01.730
[Conan Voiceover] When
I heard President Trump

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.720
had insulted Haiti in the Oval Office.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.620
The President asked,

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.470
"Why are we having all these people

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.210
"from shithole countries come here?",

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.620
referring to African countries and Haiti.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.410
The President then went on to talk about

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.270
how they needed to bring in more

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:16.440
people from places like Norway.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.740
Now I have no idea what the president

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.440
has against the people of Haiti,

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.320
but if the president doesn't like them,

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.570
they must be lovely people.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.143
[Conan Voiceover] A day later,

00:00:29.143 --> 00:00:31.460
I was exchanging dollars
for Haitian gourde,

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.490
and before I knew it,

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:33.440
I was in Port-au-Prince

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.380
receiving a warm welcome
and a bottle of rum.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.460
Now this will last me this morning.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.970
[Conan Voiceover] To
understand today's Haiti,

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:41.410
you need to know its history.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.900
This should only take a
minute and 23 seconds.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.100
Before the Europeans came,

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.760
Haiti was inhabited by the
indigenous Taíno people.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.150
Then the Spanish arrived,
conquered the Taínos,

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.120
plundered their gold,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.350
and brought in thousands
of African slaves.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.900
Then the French did the same
thing when they took over.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.473
Then in 1804,

00:00:57.473 --> 00:01:00.210
Toussaint Louverture and
Jean-Jacques Dessalines

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.380
led a slave revolt, defeated the French,

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:04.440
and the nation of Haiti was born,

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.800
but France demanded reparations,

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.400
and Haiti had to pay them
91 million gold francs.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.233
All the while,

00:01:11.233 --> 00:01:12.730
the poor black majority
fought with the small

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.700
but wealthy mulattoes, dividing Haiti.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:15.900
Until in 1915,

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.070
the US invaded to impose stability

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.360
while also removing the gold

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.900
from the Haitian National Bank.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.070
When the US withdrew,

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:23.610
Haiti was led by military juntas

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.400
and mostly corrupt presidents including

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.954
Francois "Papa Doc" Duvalier and his son,

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:31.330
Jean-Claude "Baby Doc" Duvalier
who, for the next 30 years,

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.700
siphoned hundreds of millions
of dollars out of the country,

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.440
and were followed by
a military government,

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:36.550
more appointed presidents,

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:38.250
military rulers, an elected leader,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.040
more military rulers, another election,

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.270
then a coup d'etat, a
UN peacekeeping force,

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:43.900
and more contested elections.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.110
Then a devastating earthquake which killed

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.680
hundreds of thousands of Haitians

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:50.290
followed by food shortages,
an outbreak of cholera,

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:51.940
and devastation by hurricanes.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:54.020
In short, the people of
Haiti have been dealt

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.520
the worst hand in the Western hemisphere,

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.180
but their spirit remains intact.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:00.850
I couldn't wait to get outside

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.318
and meet these wonderful people.

00:02:02.318 --> 00:02:05.720
(audience cheers)

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.230
I just bumped into this gentleman.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.063
Your name is?

00:02:08.063 --> 00:02:08.896
Kenzo.

00:02:08.896 --> 00:02:09.770
You're very funny.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:10.750
[Conan] Oh, thank you.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.230
Yeah mean, I remember
watching a clip on YouTube,

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:13.140
you and Kevin Hart.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.290
And Ice Cube.
Oh, yeah, Kevin Hart.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:16.240
Yeah, man, and I like Kevin Hart also.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.073
Oh, he's fantastic.

00:02:17.073 --> 00:02:17.906
He's the other good fellow I prefer.

00:02:17.906 --> 00:02:19.600
You know, you're much
taller than Kevin Hart.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.433
Yeah, man, I am.

00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:21.266
He comes up to here.

00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:22.440
He comes up to here on you.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.430
I watch CNN.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.290
Oh, and by the way,

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.653
on CNN, I used to watch

00:02:27.653 --> 00:02:30.210
The Situation Room with Wolf Blitzer.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:32.810
You know, I love this guy's a fan

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.720
of mine and Wolf Blitzer.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.850
You're the only guy that likes both of us.

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:39.250
Most people that like him, don't like me.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.083
Hey, how's it going?

00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:41.200
Hey, I was watching you this morning.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.033
How are you?

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:43.242
My wife made me watch you, bro.

00:02:43.242 --> 00:02:44.605
I really appreciate you saying that.

00:02:44.605 --> 00:02:47.810
Wait, why did you say my
wife made me watch you?

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.193
It shouldn't be that way.

00:02:49.193 --> 00:02:52.600
That makes it sound like
she made you do the dishes.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.300
I wouldn't mind if she made
me do the dishes as well.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.830
It's nice to meet you.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:57.663
What's your name?

00:02:57.663 --> 00:02:58.496
Nice to meet you, my name is James.

00:02:58.496 --> 00:02:59.329
James,

00:02:59.329 --> 00:03:00.240
you love Haiti?

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.640
I love Haiti.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.400
So, okay, let's talk about it.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.240
President Trump used some really

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.360
awful language about Haiti last week.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.740
He used the word shithole.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:12.070
What words would you
use to describe Haiti?

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.540
Well, I would describe Haiti
as the backyard of America.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:17.460
If it's a shithole,

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.190
then Trump should check out his backyard.

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:22.190
You see what I'm saying?

00:03:23.414 --> 00:03:24.330
That's fantastic.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.620
I haven't heard anyone say that.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.778
According to the history of this country,

00:03:27.778 --> 00:03:29.575
America has had a lot to do

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:31.930
with the condition of this country.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.370
I mean, it may not be so beautiful.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:37.360
There's trash and garbage a
lot of places, but you know,

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.990
the people of Haiti are

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.510
brilliant, intelligent
people, and loving people,

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:43.620
and well-receiving people.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.300
Creative and also really funny.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.580
Everyone I run into is really funny.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:48.440
Haitian people,

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.350
I think that's one of their strengths

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.890
because they make a
joke out of everything.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:56.661
You've got a very cool,
centered vibe, and I like that.

00:03:56.661 --> 00:03:58.560
I want to emulate you.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.500
Do some yoga.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.700
Put some yoga into your life.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:01.580
Yoga?

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.440
No, no, don't do that, don't do that.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:03.504
Why not, why not?

00:04:03.504 --> 00:04:05.750
Just sit here with your back straight,

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.870
and close your eyes.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.300
Make sure you're straight, now.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.760
Alright, and now just observe

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.406
your inhalation and your exhalation,

00:04:14.406 --> 00:04:17.800
and get intimate with
yourself, with your breathing.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:18.977
Okay, I'm intimate with myself.

00:04:18.977 --> 00:04:21.120
(laughs)

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.467
Just this morning, in fact.

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:23.850
(laughs)

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.780
You are better at foreign policy

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.270
than the President of the
United States right now.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:28.390
What's your full name?

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:29.700
My name is James Vergneau.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.430
I wish James Vergneau

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:33.370
was President of the
United States right now.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.753
I really wish that was true.

00:04:34.753 --> 00:04:35.586
That would be wonderful.

00:04:35.586 --> 00:04:36.700
[Announcer] James Vergneau believes

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.180
in men washing dishes, clean backyards,

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.010
and sitting up straight while
listening to your breath.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.990
Plus, he's been endorsed by
self-pleasurer, Conan O'Brien.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.971
So please, help make James Vergneau

00:04:47.971 --> 00:04:50.505
the next President of the United States.

00:04:50.505 --> 00:04:55.005
My name is James Vergneau,
and I approve this message.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:00.760
Apparently, there's a group
over here that's really angry.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:02.920
They saw me, they know I'm American,

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.160
and they see my camera crew.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.857
We're being told through our interpreter

00:05:06.857 --> 00:05:07.980
that when Americans come here,

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.560
they only shoot the bad
things, which obviously,

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.150
is not what we want to do.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:14.494
Maybe you can tell them the
reason I've come to Haiti

00:05:14.494 --> 00:05:16.640
(speaks in Haitian Creole)

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.370
is because I and a lot of Americans

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.225
are angry about what President Trump said.

00:05:21.225 --> 00:05:25.574
(speaks in Haitian Creole)

00:05:25.574 --> 00:05:28.808
So I wanted to come
here and show positive,

00:05:28.808 --> 00:05:31.115
great, beautiful things about Haiti.

00:05:31.115 --> 00:05:34.220
(speaks in Haitian Creole)

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.300
But I understand why
just seeing an American

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.341
right now with a camera
would make people angry.

00:05:38.341 --> 00:05:42.091
(speaks in Haitian Creole)

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:06.850
I actually wrote a speech,

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:08.260
tried to write a speech in Creole,

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:11.389
but I can't say it very well,
about my intentions here.

00:06:11.389 --> 00:06:15.139
(speaks in Haitian Creole)

00:06:53.599 --> 00:06:56.230
So you go ahead and tell Trump

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:59.350
to go find out about Dessalines.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.183
About?

00:07:00.183 --> 00:07:01.016
Dessalines.

00:07:01.016 --> 00:07:01.849
Oh, this island, yes.

00:07:01.849 --> 00:07:03.051
He doesn't listen to me, Trump.

00:07:03.051 --> 00:07:03.884
Dessalines.

00:07:03.884 --> 00:07:05.634
Oh, this island, yes.

00:07:28.928 --> 00:07:30.147
Trump is not my friend.

00:07:30.147 --> 00:07:30.980
He doesn't listen.

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.217
Jean-Jacques Dessalines.

00:07:32.217 --> 00:07:33.050
(speaks in Haitian Creole)

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:36.190
He doesn't listen to me,
but I will try and tell him.

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:38.860
(speaks in Haitian Creole)

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:40.760
Guys, I know a way we can get Trump

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:43.817
to watch this message right now, okay?

00:07:43.817 --> 00:07:48.053
(speaks in Haitian Creole)

00:07:48.053 --> 00:07:49.160
So take care of that right now

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.780
so that we know Trump watches, and bang.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:52.670
There you go.

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:55.675
Now, you say your message
right there to Trump.

00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:59.425
(speaks in Haitian Creole)

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:22.115
I'm still here, by the way, I'm just

00:08:22.115 --> 00:08:23.750
trying to participate.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:25.750
Watch what's going down.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:30.543
It's just like Thanksgiving at my house.

